# What the build context must not carry.
#
# Two separate costs, and the second one is the expensive kind.
#
# Size: without this file every `docker compose build` ships the whole working tree to the daemon,
# which today is 5.8 GB of Rust build output no image references. On a 2-OCPU VM that is the
# difference between a build and an afternoon.
#
# Correctness: `node_modules` is copied in AFTER `bun install` has already resolved the workspace,
# so a host tree's symlinks — pointing at macOS paths that do not exist in the image — land on top
# of a correct install. The build then fails somewhere unrelated, with an error about a module.
#
# And `.env` is here because an image is a thing you push. A secret that reaches a layer has been
# published, whether or not any process ever reads it.

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.DS_Store

desktop/src-tauri/target
desktop/src-tauri/gen

# Regenerated during the build from the tenant package, so a host copy can only be stale.
app/src/lib/generated

.git
.github
.logs
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
